# ^ The upstream official-pikafish/Pikafish `jieqi_old` commit the prod image builds
# (railpack build step reads the first line; this comment is ignored).
#
# Pinned 2026-08-28. Before this, the build was `git clone --depth 1 -b jieqi_old`,
# so every deploy rebuilt the analysis engine from whatever branch tip existed that
# day. That is a reproducibility hole with teeth: whole-game analysis is cached by
# (room, engine, depth), and the engine component was a hand-maintained version
# string that knew nothing about the binary. Two deploys either side of an upstream
# commit would therefore file evals from two different engines under one identical
# key, with nothing to detect it. The same shape applies to the xiangqi Pikafish
# build on the following railpack line, which is still unpinned; pinning it would
# also change the live xiangqi bot, so it is deliberately left for its own change.
#
# The short form of this SHA is part of JIEQI_ANALYSIS_ENGINE_ID, so moving this pin
# invalidates jieqi analysis caches on purpose rather than silently reusing them.
# jieqi-engine-ref.test.ts fails if the two drift apart.
#
# Bumping: check out the new ref, rebuild, and expect a full recompute of every
# jieqi review. There is no way to keep the old rows: they were produced by a
# different engine, which is the whole point of keying on this.
